---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="SPD Certification Tracking Software | CRCST & CBSPD | Certivue"
  description="Track CRCST, CBSPD, CIS, and CHL certifications, monitor expirations, store certificates, and manage renewals — certification tracking built for sterile processing departments."
  canonical="https://certivue.com/certification-tracking"
>
  <section style="padding-top:140px; padding-bottom:64px; padding-left:20px; padding-right:20px;">
    <div style="max-width:760px; margin:0 auto;">
      <h1 style="color:#fff; font-size:clamp(32px, 6vw, 48px); font-weight:500; letter-spacing:-1px; line-height:1.15; margin:0 0 20px;">
        Sterile Processing Certification Tracking Software
      </h1>
      <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:17px; line-height:1.6; margin:0;">
        Keep every technician's certifications current, documented, and audit-ready. Certivue tracks CRCST, CBSPD, CIS, CHL, and other SPD credentials, flags expirations before they lapse, and gives managers a clear view of department-wide compliance.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding:0 20px 80px;">
    <div style="max-width:760px; margin:0 auto; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:48px;">

      <div>
        <h2 style="color:#fff; font-size:26px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 12px; letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
          Why certification tracking matters in the SPD
        </h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0;">
          Sterile processing certifications carry continuing-education requirements and renewal deadlines, and a single lapsed credential can put a department out of compliance. Tracking dozens of technicians' certifications across spreadsheets and email reminders is error-prone — expirations slip, certificates get lost, and gaps only surface during a survey.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="color:#fff; font-size:26px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 12px; letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
          Every credential, tracked and documented
        </h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0;">
          Add each technician's certifications directly to their employee profile, with the credential type, issue and expiration dates, and a copy of the certificate uploaded and stored securely. Managers can add, edit, renew, or remove certifications from one place, and every certificate document is a click away when a surveyor asks.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="color:#fff; font-size:26px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 12px; letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
          Expirations you see coming
        </h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0;">
          Certivue surfaces upcoming certification expirations so renewals happen on schedule instead of after a lapse. Instead of tracking renewal dates by memory, managers get a clear picture of what's current, what's expiring soon, and what needs action.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="color:#fff; font-size:26px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 12px; letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
          A renewal workflow that keeps managers in control
        </h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0;">
          Technicians can submit certification renewal requests when they complete continuing education or re-certify, and managers review and approve them before the record updates. This keeps certification data accurate while giving technicians a way to keep their own credentials moving.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="color:#fff; font-size:26px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 12px; letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
          Department-wide compliance at a glance
        </h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0;">
          The role-based compliance view shows certification status across every active role in the department, so leaders can see at a glance where the team stands. Compliance stops being a fire drill and becomes something you monitor continuously.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div style="text-align:center; background:#161820; border:0.5px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); border-radius:12px; padding:48px;">
        <h2 style="color:#fff; font-size:26px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 10px; letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
          See certification tracking in action
        </h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:15px; margin-bottom:28px;">
          Give your SPD team one system to track, store, and renew every credential.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/#demo"
          style="display:inline-block; background:#22d3c8; color:#0f1117; font-weight:500; border-radius:8px; padding:10px 22px; text-decoration:none; font-size:15px;"
        >
          Request a demo
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
